1) Stay out of the mines until you have the armor/tools/pet to not die.
 Many classes attract a lot of fights.  My recommended pet size for the
mines is 'large'.
2) Get a bunch of darts.  Make sure they're not cursed.  Throw them in
shops.  This is a good way to find mimics until you can get a floating
eye and a blindfold/towel.  Also note that mimics are super slow so you
can use the whack-'n'-backup technique.
3) Collect daggers.  Get experienced at dagger and throw often.  Find a
dagger that isn't cursed and doesn't stack with the others and wield
it.  Just keep the quarter-matchstick as backup.
4) You should be able to find a [studded] leather armor, some kind of
helmet, and some kind of boots.  Gloves or small shield are a bonus.
Death drops and pet managment should get you an AC of 5 or lower
without going too deep.  Enchantment is a bonus (if you can find it).
If you find enchant armor, put it on your CoMR.  The shield and the
helmet will cut your spell success rate, but they're worth it for the
armor class.
5) If your power is at 100% and you are not at XL1, and you know first
level spells like protection/jumping/detectmonsters, cast them for fun.
 Get out of unskilled class and get your fail rate down.  (Why do I
like jumping and detect monsters so much?  They're practice for casting
haste self and identify.)
6) If you know sleep, always cast that first before beginning melee.
7) Check what you wrote when you wrote the E-word.  If you write with
your fingers, there is a significant chance of making a spelling error.
 You may have to write it over again.  If you want to write with a word
or gem, you have to do it in advance and then back up to that location
as a safe spot.



